Academic freedom is politically constrained, and self-censorship among faculty is common. University professors and teachers have reportedly been hired or dismissed due to their political affiliations.
Freedom of private discussion is limited. The government uses informants and electronic surveillance to monitor members of the [OPPOSITION PARTY], [NGO], and journalists, including the few members of the foreign press in [COUNTRY]. Critics of the government are subject to arbitrary arrest, physical abuse, and trumped-up charges.

